<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian sugar crush - week to June 28.</title>
<headline>Australian sugar crush - week to June 28.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's sugar cane crush totalled 1,255,574 tonnes in the week ended June 28, bringing the crush so far this year to 2.53 million tonnes, grower organisation CANEGROWERS said.</p>
<p>This is behind the 2.59 million tonnes crushed at the same time last year. CANEGROWERS reported for crushing week four of the 1997 season that average commercial cane sugar (ccs) content was 12.25 percent.</p>
<p>The figures do not include cane crushed in the Ord River region of Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Australian sugar cane crush by region for the week ended June 21 as reported by CANEGROWERS in tonnes.</p>
<p>CCS = Commercial Cane Sugar (sugar content percent)-</p>
<p>			Crushed   Crushed  CCS	 CCS</p>
<p>			This wk   to Date  this wk   to date</p>
<p> North Qld	 301,526    446,707   11.65     11.59</p>
<p> Burdekin	  263,193    791,374   13.29     13.01</p>
<p> Central Qld     467,726    955,457   12.39     12.36</p>
<p> South Qld	 148,199    148,199   12.32     12.32</p>
<p> Queensland    1,180,644  2,341,737   12.39     12.43</p>
<p> N.South Wales    74,930    192,744   10.04     10.07</p>
<p> Australia     1,255,574  2,534,481   12.25     12.25</p>
<p>				   YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Queensland    1,242,680   2,590,144   12.05     11.86</p>
<p> Australia     1,242,680   2,590,144   12.05     11.86</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Summary - Total cane crushed 39.604 million tonnes (Qld 37.217 million, NSW 2.387 million), sugar produced 5.442 million tonnes 94 n.t., (Qld 5.156 million, NSW 285,616), sugar content (CCS) 13.50 percent (Qld 13.62 percent, NSW 11.63 percent).</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
